    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>SMNTCS To The Top Block adds a link that takes visitors back to the top of the page. Place it anywhere in a page, post or custom post type, for example at the end of a long article. Clicking the link scrolls smoothly to the top.</p>\n<p>Add the block in the block editor, type your own label and align it left, centre or right. The block works with block themes and with classic themes that call <code>wp_body_open</code>.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Align the link left, centre or right.</li>\n<li>Adjust the label according to your needs.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code> directory.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the <code>Plugins</code> menu in WordPress.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.6 (2025.03.23)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 6.8</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.5.0 (2023.10.21)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Bump version to trigger WordPress.org deploy action</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.0 (2023.10.21)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 6.4</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.3.0 (2023.03.04)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested up to WordPress 6.2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.2.0 (2022.07.12)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Update screenshots</li>\n<li>Update tags</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.1.0 (2022.07.07)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add build folder to repo due to WordPress.org deploy action</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0 (2022.07.01)</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Adds a jump to the top link to your pages, posts or custom post types.",
    "description": "<p>SMNTCS To The Top Block adds a link that takes visitors back to the top of the page. Place it anywhere in a page, post or custom post type, for example at the end of a long article. Clicking the link scrolls smoothly to the top.</p>\n<p>Add the block in the block editor, type your own label and align it left, centre or right. The block works with block themes and with classic themes that call <code>wp_body_open</code>.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Align the link left, centre or right.</li>\n<li>Adjust the label according to your needs.</li>\n</ul>\n",
